# Build context for infra/docker/Dockerfile.api (BuildKit picks
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore up automatically; it takes precedence over a
# .dockerignore at the context root, which this repository cannot have — 00 §5.2
# allows no such top-level dot entry, see scripts/check-layout.sh).
#
# The context is the repository root. The image needs Directory.Build.props,
# Directory.Packages.props, global.json, nuget.config, src/ (with the committed
# packages.lock.json files) and the two repository directories the shipped
# projects read AT BUILD TIME:
#
#   contracts/   contracts/rls-exceptions.txt is an EmbeddedResource of
#                BuildingBlocks.Persistence (02.6.1-T1.4), and its absence fails
#                the compile (measured 2026-09-27);
#   migrations/  Persistence globs migrations/*.sql and bakes the greatest file
#                name into assembly metadata as the expected journal head
#                (01.1.2-T1.3). A missing directory would not fail the build — it
#                would silently bake the "(none)" sentinel and make every ready
#                probe fail — so it stays in the context.
#
# Everything below is host state: it must never enter a layer and must not be
# tarred into the context. The three Dockerfile.<name>.dockerignore files are
# kept byte-identical; scripts/build-images.sh --check-pins fails when they drift.
.git
.github
.spectral.yaml
artifacts
TestResults
docs
plans
tests
node_modules
**/node_modules
apps/web/dist
package-lock.json
**/bin
**/obj
**/*.user
**/*.md
.DS_Store
# Git-ignored host state that is otherwise tarred into the context (measured
# 2026-09-27: `.env.dev`, `.local/` and `apps/web/playwright-report/` were all in
# the context until these lines were added). `.env.dev` is the one that matters:
# scripts/dev/up.sh writes real per-role passwords into it (00 §5.7 S3). The
# Dockerfiles COPY named paths only, so none of this reaches a layer — but the
# context is uploaded to the builder, so it must not carry credentials either.
.env*
.local
.husky
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/*.tsbuildinfo
